Previous 4.4 (SourceForge SVN trunk r1847) — do not reserve imaginary
window-manager decorations when there is no window manager.

Screen_SetWindowSize() asks SDL how thick the window's border is and, when SDL
cannot answer, assumes a decorated desktop: 50 px of titlebar, 50 px of bottom
frame and 25 px each side. It then shrinks the emulated NeXT screen until it
fits inside `usable bounds - borders`. On the gallery's bridge kiosk there is no
window manager at all, so SDL_GetWindowBordersSize() always returns false and
the 1120x832 MegaPixel display was scaled to 0.971 — a non-integer downscale
that resamples every glyph of a 1-bit-crisp Display PostScript UI, and destroys
the 1:1 host-pixel-to-guest-pixel mapping this tile's relative pointer path
depends on.

Measured on the tile, both runs on a 1120x832 X root:
  before   stderr "SDL screen scale: 0.971", window 1088x808, blurred text
  after    no scale line, window 1120x832, exact pixels, no letterbox

A window with no decorations genuinely has zero-thickness borders, so zero is
also the honest answer for any WM-less session.

Apply with: patch -p0 -d <previous-code checkout> < this file

Index: src/gui-sdl/sdlscreen.c
===================================================================
--- src/gui-sdl/sdlscreen.c	(revision 1847)
+++ src/gui-sdl/sdlscreen.c	(working copy)
@@ -379,8 +379,10 @@
 		int top, left, bottom, right;
 		float hscale, wscale;
 		if (SDL_GetWindowBordersSize(sdlWindow, &top, &left, &bottom, &right) == false) {
-			top = bottom = 50;
-			left = right = 25;
+			/* No window manager: the window really has no decorations,
+			 * so do not shrink the emulated screen to make room for
+			 * imaginary ones (kernel-hive bridge kiosk). */
+			top = bottom = left = right = 0;
 		} else if (!ConfigureParams.Screen.bShowStatusbar) {
 			bottom += 24; /* make sure there is enough space to show statusbar */
 		}
